Empowering Discoveries in Oncology Research\
\
CDI Labs Canada and CDI Labs offer unique and empowering research tools and services that are being used to advance the understanding of immunotherapy response and inform therapeutic development.\
\
Chronic viral infections are known to impact cancer patient outcomes. VirScan\'99 Viral PhIP-Seq (https://www.cdilabs.ca/products/virscan-phip-seq) antibody profiling* from CDI Labs Canada has been used in research highlighting that CMV-induced T cell senescence is associated with poorer outcomes in patients with advanced NSCLC treated by checkpoint blockade immunotherapy1.\
\
VirScan allows researchers to determine what antibodies were created by an individual\'92s unique history of viral exposures. PhIP-Seq is the highest-coverage antigen-specific assay yet developed and enables simultaneous epitope-level antibody profiling versus most vertebrate viruses.\
\
The HuProt\'99 Human Proteome Microarray (https://www.cdilabs.com/products/huprot-microarray) from CDI Labs has been used to identify autoantibody signatures that have the potential to predict both disease recurrence and immune-related adverse events in melanoma patients treated with checkpoint inhibitor adjuvant immunotherapy2. HuProt was also used to support findings that indicate that immunotherapies that boost both coordinated B and T cell responses against human ovarian cancer - an immunogenic disease that is currently resistant to checkpoint inhibitors - are likely to show increased therapeutic benefit3.\
\
With over 21,000 GST-purified, full-length human proteins and isoform variants, the HuProt Proteome Microarray is revolutionizing cancer research by unveiling new biomarkers and therapeutic targets that could potentially transform patient care in immuno-oncology.\
\
* VirScan is provided exclusively by CDI Labs Canada.\
